WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.322 --> 00:00:01.780
SPEAKER: Welcome
to "Cloud Minute."

00:00:01.780 --> 00:00:03.660
Today I am going to show you
how to create a managed instance

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:04.770
group from the command line.

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:07.270
I'll be using Cloud Shell, but
you can use your own terminal

00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:08.400
if you'd prefer.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:12.570
First we need to create
an instance template.

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:15.260
Name your template.

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:18.470
Set the machine type.

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:19.790
And set a boot disk size.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:26.697
Additional flags can
be found in the Help.

00:00:26.697 --> 00:00:29.196
If you want to see what's in a
given template, use Describe.

00:00:34.229 --> 00:00:36.020
Now you can create a
managed instance group

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:36.811
from your template.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:42.060
Name your group.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:44.310
Specify the template.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:47.500
And specify the group size.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:50.300
Now you've created a managed
instance group using gcloud.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:52.208
Check out our other
Cloud Minutes.

